  "equipment_type": "Boiler controller gateway (ProtoNode)",
  "applies_to": "Cosmogas boilers with the Argus managing/standalone control, including up to four dependent burners, through a ProtoNode RER (BACnet) gateway.",
  "summary": "A ProtoNode RER (FPC-N34) reads a Cosmogas Argus managing or standalone boiler over Modbus RTU and serves it on BACnet MS/TP or BACnet IP. The 41 objects cover heating and DHW setpoints and modes, outdoor-reset parameters, supply/return/DHW/flue temperatures, firing rate, flame current, water pressure, error codes and per-burner state, status, error and firing rate for four dependent burners, plus a control register that must be set before writes.",
  "bacnet_transport": [
    "BACnet IP",
    "BACnet MS/TP"
  ],
  "firmware": null,
  "default_device_instance": null,
  "access_inferred": true,
  "notes": [
    "The table gives no read/write column; access is inferred from object type (AV/MV writable, AI read-only).",
    "Write MV 95 Control Register = 1 before changing any value.",
    "Temperatures and pressure follow the unit flags in AV 1 (°C/°F, bar/psi); only the two setpoint ranges are stated in °F.",
    "Device instance = Node_Offset (default 50,000) + the boiler's Modbus Node-ID.",
    "Mestek hosts this guide under RBI Infinite Energy 2 water heaters; the guide itself names only Cosmogas Argus.",
    "Dependent_3 Satus is spelled as printed."
  ],
  "source": {
    "title": "ProtoNode RER and ProtoNode LER Startup Guide - For Interfacing Cosmogas Products: Argus Managing/Standalone Boiler and Dependent Boiler",
    "doc_number": "Instruction 62403594 R08",
    "revision_date": "Jun. 06, 2017",
    "url": "https://www.literature.mestek.com/dms/RBI%20Water%20Heaters/Infinite%20Energy%202/ProtoCessor-FieldServer%20IOM%20(R08).pdf"
  },
  "integration": {
    "summary": "Set the boilers to Modbus RTU 9600 8-N-1 with unique Node-IDs, wire them to the ProtoNode, select BACnet MS/TP or BACnet IP on the S DIP switches and run auto-discovery. Before any write, set MV 95 to 1, then write setpoints and modes.",
